      "problem": "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=0.4$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=\\frac{3}{5}.$ Find $\\text{Var}[X+Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X\\pm Y]=\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X+Y]=0.4+\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{3}{5}=1.\n$$",
